the Largest Metal Asteroid in the Solar System. Photo courtesy of Spacepoint.</p>\n        \n        \n            <p>NASA</p>\n        \n    \n\n        \n            \n    <p><img src=\"https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims4/default/1739d24/2147483647/strip/true/crop/3000x1848+0+0/resize/880x542!/quality/90/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Ff4%2Fc7%2F095104c849a48c56a8c075567b3d%2Fpsyche-launch.jpg\" alt=\"Psyche launch in 2023. Photo courtesy of Spacepoint.\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" width=\"880\" height=\"542\" /> \n            \n        \n    </p>\n    \n        <p>2 of 4\n             — Psyche Launch.jpg\n        </p>\n        \n            <p>Psyche launch in 2023. Photo courtesy of Spacepoint.</p>\n        \n        \n            <p>John Winkopp</p>\n        \n    \n\n        \n            \n    <p><img src=\"https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims4/default/b3f284c/2147483647/strip/true/crop/1442x888+0+49/resize/880x542!/quality/90/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F19%2F12%2F3f8aa7b84e0ca1e675602bd0140e%2Fpsyche-image-of-mars-during-its-flyby.png\" alt=\"The Psyche spacecraft flies by Mars. Photo courtesy of Spacepoint.\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" width=\"880\" height=\"542\" /> \n            \n        \n    </p>\n    \n        <p>3 of 4\n             — Psyche Image of Mars during its flyby.png\n        </p>\n        \n            <p> The Psyche spacecraft flies by Mars. Photo courtesy of Spacepoint.</p>\n        \n        \n            <p>NASA</p>\n        \n    \n\n        \n            \n    <p><img src=\"https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims4/default/ff5d589/2147483647/strip/true/crop/1820x1121+0+1128/resize/880x542!/quality/90/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F13%2F9e%2Ff605a8dd43848cb305b74924a387%2Fdr-ben-weiss-with-psyche-in-the-clean-room.png\" alt=\"Dr Ben Weiss, MIT and Psyche mission Deputy Principle Investigator.\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" width=\"880\" height=\"542\" /> \n            \n        \n    </p>\n    \n        <p>4 of 4\n             — Dr Ben Weiss with Psyche in the Clean Room.png\n        </p>\n        \n            <p>Dr Ben Weiss, MIT and Psyche mission Deputy Principle Investigator. </p>\n        \n        \n            <p>Photo courtesy of Spacepoint.</p>\n        \n    \n\n        \n    \n\n\n                                \n                            \n                            \n\n\n                            \n\n                            \n                                        <p>Have you ever wondered what an asteroid is made of? Well, <a href=\"https://www.benweiss.mit.edu/about\" rel=\"noopener nofollow\" target=\"_blank\"><u>Dr. Ben Weiss</u></a>, the Chair of Planetary Science at MIT, has been wondering about that for a very long time. He <a href=\"https://www.nasa.gov/wp-content/uploads/2025/04/weissbp-11-15-23.pdf?emrc=efe1df\" rel=\"noopener nofollow\" target=\"_blank\"><u>studies paleomagnetism</u></a> and he’s the deputy principal investigator for NASA’s <a href=\"https://science.nasa.gov/mission/psyche/\" rel=\"noopener nofollow\" target=\"_blank\"><u>Psyche</u></a> mission.</p><p>The goal is to study the <a href=\"https://science.nasa.gov/mission/psyche/mission-overview/\" rel=\"noopener nofollow\" target=\"_blank\"><u>asteroid called Psyche</u></a> to find out if it’s made of metal and if it <a href=\"https://science.nasa.gov/mission/psyche/science/\" rel=\"noopener nofollow\" target=\"_blank\"><u>could be the leftover core</u></a> of a baby planet. The spacecraft has already made a <a href=\"https://science.nasa.gov/blogs/psyche/2026/07/17/nasas-psyche-mission-delivers-mars-flyby-data-time-lapse-video/\" rel=\"noopener nofollow\" target=\"_blank\"><u>flyby of Mars</u></a>.</p><p>Dr. Weiss is coming to JUMP in Boise on Saturday, Sept. 26 for <a href=\"https://www.spacepoint.org/event-details-registration/interplanetary-life-2026\" rel=\"noopener nofollow\" target=\"_blank\"><u>Interplanetary Life - March of the Robots</u></a>!</p><p>When we heard about the March of the Robots, we had to know more, so we asked <a href=\"https://www.spacepoint.org/\" rel=\"noopener nofollow\" target=\"_blank\"><u>Spacepoint</u></a> if they could help us get in touch with some of the people involved with the missions and they connected us with Dr. Weiss and <a href=\"https://www.boisestatepublicradio.org/show/idaho-matters/2025-02-04/nonprofit-space\" rel=\"noopener nofollow\" target=\"_blank\"><u>Kyle Averill</u></a>, the president and co-founder of Spacepoint.</p><p>Find out more about other robot missions on our <a href=\"https://www.boisestatepublicradio.org/space-robots\" rel=\"noopener nofollow\" target=\"_blank\"><u>Space Robots</u></a> page!</p>\n                                    \n                        \n\n                        \n\n\n\n\n                        \n                            \n                        \n\n                        \n                            \n        \n            \n        \n\n        \n            \n                \n            \n\n            <p>\n                \n                    As Senior Producer of our live daily talk show Idaho Matters, I’m able to indulge my love of storytelling and share all kinds of information (I was probably a Town Crier in a past life). My career has allowed me to learn something new everyday and to share that knowledge with all my friends on the radio.\n                \n            </p>"
}
